# Git and local tooling
.git
.gitignore
**/.nx/cache
# Rewritten by every nx invocation (~19MB). CI runs codegen before `docker build`,
# so without this it lands in the manifests stage's `COPY . .` layer and gets
# re-exported to the layer cache on every build. Bloat only — it cannot bust the
# npm ci layer, which is keyed on the extracted package.json set.
**/.nx/workspace-data
**/.cache

# Rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Dev artifacts
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Not needed for app image builds
docs/
packages/e2e/playwright-report/
output.json
output-worker-graph.json

# Compose/Makefile are not part of the build context payload
docker-compose/
Makefile

# Deploy/runtime plumbing the IMAGE BUILD never reads. These sit under infra/,
# which the Dockerfile copies wholesale (`COPY infra infra`) BEFORE `COPY apps`
# and `RUN npx nx build`. Without these exclusions, editing a deploy script
# invalidates that layer and every layer after it, forcing a full application
# rebuild for a change the build cannot even see — measured at ~4min of wasted
# arm64 build time on an infra-only PR.
#
# Keep excluding ONLY things the build does not read. infra/config/{nx,tsconfig,jest}
# MUST stay in the context: nx.json extends infra/config/nx/nx.json and
# tsconfig.base.json extends infra/config/tsconfig/tsconfig.base.json, so
# excluding those breaks the build outright.
infra/scripts/
infra/config/docker-compose/
infra/config/localstack/
